0 Medullary excipulum 3-layered, with a hyphal middle layer (textura intricata). Ascomata small to large, sessile or stipitate.0224603
0 Medullary excipulum I-layered, cellular (lextura gIobulosa or gIobuIosa-angularis). Ascomata small,< 2 cm diam., usually sessile (sometimes substipitate).0225705
0 Ascomata large, up to 15 cm diam., deeply cupulate (usually even at maturity), with a pale ochreousyellowish disc, vesiculose due to the hymenium separating from the underlying flesh. Spores 19-26 x 10-14  m. On manure or heavily manured soils. 034680 Peziza vesicuIosa0
0 Ascomata smaller, shallow-cupulate or flattened, with an olive tawny-brown, more or less regular and usually darker disc.0347904
0 Ascomata sessile, up to 4 cm diam. Spores 18-20 x 10-11 µm, often with de Bary bubbles and an easily loosening perisporium. On equine dung but also on humus, bare or burnt soil. 0478100 Peziza azorica0
0 Ascomata long stipitate. Disc up to 2.5 cm diam. Spores 14-18 x 8-10 flm (LE GAL, 1941; DONADINI, 1979), 18-22 x 11-12 µm (BOUDIER, 1905-1910). without de Bary bubbles and an easily loosening perisporium. On humus or moist ground, sometimes on heavily manured soil. 0479110 Peziza asterigma0
